    "updated_at": "2026-04-14T09:24:31Z",
    "body": "> The worst thing one can do is make a decision on behalf of the user without even asking them, with no way for them to accomplish what they want! Maybe 15-20 years ago, people didn't know that geolocation could be encoded in their photos, but now **EVERYBODY** knows this!\n\nAnd people EXPECT that the information is kept. It's really hard to convey that the information they see on their phone is lost when they upload it to the web. It's always expected there is an error in the app. I've been through the same issue with iOS in 2019 https://stackoverflow.com/questions/57942150/file-upload-and-exif-in-mobile-safari",
